{"kind":"text","seq":58,"text":"Round 1 done — banked score is the current build.\n\n**Best: 95-piece steel twister — excitement 6.83, intensity 9.92, nausea 5.99, similarity 0.39 (no penalty).**\n\nLayout: 30 m chain lift → 60° plunge → **Immelmann** (half loop into a corkscrew rollout) → vertical loop → banked sweep south → **double corkscrew barrel-roll pair** → a snaking run of six airtime hills → banked hook back into the station. 589 m long, 12 drops, 4 inversions, 77 ticks of airtime.\n\nWhat the iterations taught me, in case it's useful next round:\n- Inversion count is the dominant intensity lever — going 4 → 6 inversions sent intensity from 9.9 to **14.9** and collapsed excitement to 2.15.\n- Drop height is a weak excitement lever (18 m → 30 m bought only +0.06) but an expensive intensity one.\n- Airtime hills and track length are the cheap wins: they added ~+0.4 excitement for almost no intensity.\n- The build is parked right at the ceiling (9.92 vs the ~10 cliff), so any further gain has to come from *buying* intensity headroom — softening the drop pull-out or the loop entry speed — before spending it on more length."}
